{
  "description": "A node's whole life on the wire (docs/control-port.md#fixtures; the phases slice 3a has): node.added (added), then a node.state for every change of any health member, each carrying state, phase, since (when the phase began: it moves only with the phase), wanted and blockLost, and cause, waitingFor and reason when the health has them. A stop and a start (no graphFile.changed or node.updated: they edit nothing); a restart (stopping with cause restarting, its reply, then configuring with cause action); a disable and an enable (node.updated with applied and disabled; stopping with cause disabling, then disabled; configuring with cause enabling); node.start on a disabled node refused node-disabled; a node configured while stopped (it rests stopped again); a node added disabled (node.added says disabled, and its first node.state says it again, for a client that reads a state only from node.state); a failed node stopped (one node.state, wanted stopped), retried by node.start and by node.restart (applied retry); a restart during a restart (unchanged); a block lost (blockLost) and the refusals not-restartable block-lost; a name added back waiting for its older node (waitingFor older-node) and refused not-restartable not-started; a removal (node.stopped, then node.gone; ignored by the client, which dropped the node at node.removed); node.restart of a disabled node refused node-disabled; node.stop on a node still configuring (one node.state, the same phase, wanted stopped), which rests stopped once configured. Every reply comes after the node.state its request caused in that turn.",
